{"nodes": [{"id": "pivot_pivot_md", "label": "PIVOT.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "pivot_witness", "label": "Witness", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Renamed from Ghost Work. A witness testifies, and a claim without corroboration isn't testimony, it's rumor \u2014 the name encodes the confirm-against-a-second-source mechanic that is the project's core mechanism."}, {"id": "pivot_ghost_work", "label": "Ghost Work", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Original project name before the rename to Witness."}, {"id": "pivot_the_pivot", "label": "The pivot: make the database the detector", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In the original architecture the source-degradation claim (restricting to one connector produces a confident, wrong performance review) is unverifiable \u2014 a judge has to take on faith that no hidden code branch like a source-name conditional faked it. Moving attribution into Postgres temporal joins and gating every read through views keyed on run.enabled_sources makes degradation a structural property of the schema instead of a promise of discipline, so the demo cannot cheat even if it wanted to. InsForge ends up holding the two things the project cannot fake: what counts as proof, and who is allowed to see it."}, {"id": "pivot_confirm_attributions_function", "label": "confirm_attributions(run_id)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Postgres function implementing Stage 5 rules (a) and (b) as temporal SQL joins (e.g. joining ticket_state where the assignee differs from the message author and the ticket closed within the confirmation window after the message) \u2014 turns attribution into a temporal join rather than an LLM judgment call, and is the core of the demo running inside InsForge."}, {"id": "pivot_source_scoped_views", "label": "Source-scoped views (degradation guarantee)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "visible_source_event, visible_ticket_state, etc. are each filtered by the run's enabled_sources so disabling a source empties the table from the query's point of view \u2014 the 'must degrade for real, not fake the output' requirement is satisfied by construction rather than by code discipline."}, {"id": "pivot_classification_cache", "label": "Classification cache", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keyed on sha256(body) so classification is source-independent; without it the live toggle demo would require re-classifying hundreds of messages on stage with Pipeshift latency deciding whether the demo passes. Makes the second run return in under a second, which is what makes the live re-run demo physically possible."}, {"id": "pivot_rls_auth", "label": "RLS + Auth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Own-data / manager-of-reports visibility enforced via auth.uid() and a SECURITY DEFINER team-membership helper, so the ethics answer to 'isn't this dangerous' is a database guarantee rather than a promise about the UI."}, {"id": "pivot_storage_snapshots", "label": "Storage \u2014 run snapshots", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Raw HydraDB pull per run dumped to a bucket so runs replay deterministically from snapshot; covers the brief's 'cache one successful full run as demo fallback' and insures against venue wifi failure."}, {"id": "pivot_pgvector_fuzzy_resolution", "label": "pgvector fuzzy reference resolution", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Embeds messages and ticket titles and cosine-matches them so references like 'the auth timeout thing' resolve to a ticket even without a regex-matchable ID \u2014 meaningfully raises recall since most real Slack unblocks don't cite a ticket ID."}, {"id": "pivot_realtime_run_stream", "label": "Realtime \u2014 live run stream", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "run_stage_event insert triggers realtime.publish to a channel so pipeline stages fire live on screen. The brief lists 'no dashboard' as a non-goal for time-budget reasons, not design reasons; framed as the most watchable thing buildable for the cost."}, {"id": "pivot_schedules", "label": "Schedules (nightly run)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nightly scheduled run against the RocketRide endpoint, cheap coverage worth the minutes."}, {"id": "pivot_secrets", "label": "Secrets management", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HydraDB / Pipeshift keys referenced from edge functions \u2014 correct practice regardless of the demo."}, {"id": "pivot_edge_function_report", "label": "Edge function (report endpoint)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Public read-only report endpoint so the report is fetchable without RocketRide being awake."}, {"id": "pivot_branch_workflow", "label": "Branch workflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Apply the risky RLS migration on a backend branch first, merge when green."}, {"id": "pivot_person_table", "label": "person table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "pivot_identity_claim_table", "label": "identity_claim table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Entity resolution is never clean; keeps the claims and their evidence, not just the winning merge."}, {"id": "pivot_source_event_table", "label": "source_event table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Normalized landing table for everything HydraDB returns."}, {"id": "pivot_ticket_state_table", "label": "ticket_state table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The second source that makes confirmation possible."}, {"id": "pivot_reference_table", "label": "reference table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "pivot_classification_table", "label": "classification table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keyed by content_hash, not by message, so classifications survive re-runs."}, {"id": "pivot_attribution_table", "label": "attribution table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "pivot_run_table", "label": "run table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "pivot_run_stage_event_table", "label": "run_stage_event table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Realtime source for live per-run stage progress."}, {"id": "pivot_confirm_window_hours", "label": "confirm_window_hours run parameter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lives on the run, not in code. The brief's 48h/24h are guesses that may yield zero confirmations on small data; widening the window live without a redeploy is the difference between a demo and an apology."}, {"id": "pivot_reference_method_field", "label": "reference.method field", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Records whether a citation came from regex or vector match, so when the tool claims an artifact is evidence it can say how it found it."}, {"id": "pivot_divergence_formula_bug", "label": "Divergence formula bug (low-visible people)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "invisible / (visible + invisible) breaks on low-visible people \u2014 a new hire with two Slack messages and zero PRs scores 1.0 and tops the ranking. Fix: require a minimum of 2 confirmed attributions before a person is rankable."}, {"id": "pivot_stage6_score_contradiction", "label": "Stage 6 contradicts the pitch", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The project promises 'the result isn't a score' but Stage 6 ranks by a computed score. Fix: keep divergence as an internal sort key and never render the number, since a rendered score risks being screenshotted into a real performance review."}, {"id": "pivot_gmail_source", "label": "Gmail source (contributes nothing)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Expected to contribute nothing but kept in the toggle array because four toggleable sources makes the degradation demo richer; no logic gets built for it, and the team says so plainly if asked."}, {"id": "pivot_risk_zero", "label": "Risk zero", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The demo requires at least one Slack message referencing a ticket assigned to someone else that closed inside the window. If that pair doesn't exist in the synced HydraDB data, checking must happen first thing in the morning, while widening the window or seeding a fixture is still cheap."}, {"id": "pivot_build_order", "label": "Build order (PIVOT)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "pivot_fallback_drop_pipeshift", "label": "Fallback: drop Pipeshift entirely", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If behind schedule, fall back to regex-only reference extraction with rules (a) and (b) unchanged; the attribution engine and degradation guarantee both survive because they never depended on the LLM classification step."}, {"id": "pivot_demo_script_section", "label": "The demo (PIVOT)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "pivot_maria_eng412_example", "label": "Maria unblocked Chen on ENG-412 (example finding)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Illustrative confirmed finding used to demonstrate both the confirmation mechanism (Slack message references ENG-412, assigned to Chen, closed 2h14m later) and the degradation break (same endpoint restricted to Slack only shows Maria with zero confirmed contributions)."}, {"id": "pivot_thesis_claim", "label": "Thesis: restrict to one connector -> confident wrong review", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The original brief's central claim, used as the opening blockquote of 'The spark': scoping the tool to one connector doesn't make the answer go blank, it produces a confident, wrong performance review. Repeated on stage as 'your engineering dashboard is lying to you.'"}], "edges": [{"source": "pivot_pivot_md", "target": "pivot_witness", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_witness", "target": "pivot_ghost_work", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_pivot_md", "target": "pivot_the_pivot", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_the_pivot", "target": "pivot_thesis_claim", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_the_pivot", "target": "pivot_confirm_attributions_function", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_the_pivot", "target": "pivot_source_scoped_views", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_the_pivot", "target": "pivot_rls_auth", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_the_pivot", "target": "pivot_classification_cache", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_the_pivot", "target": "pivot_storage_snapshots", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PIVOT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pivot_confirm_attributions_function", "target": "pivot_ticket_state_table", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, 